    "engine": "jupyter",
    "markdown": "---\ngd-head-tags:\n  - >-\n    `<script type=\"application/ld+json\">[{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"SoftwareSourceCode\", \"name\": \"EdgeCase\", \"description\":\n    \"High-performance graph analysis library\", \"codeRepository\":\n    \"https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase\", \"license\":\n    \"https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT\", \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"documentation\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"programmingLanguage\": {\"@type\":\n    \"ComputerLanguage\", \"name\": \"Python\"}}, {\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"WebPage\", \"name\": \"Graph.delete_node - EdgeCase\", \"isPartOf\":\n    {\"@type\": \"WebSite\", \"name\": \"EdgeCase\"}, \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase/reference/Graph.delete_node.html\"}]</script>`{=html}\nopen-graph:\n  title: >-\n    [Graph.delete_node()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n    .doc-label-method} | EdgeCase\n  description: Delete a node from the graph.\ntwitter-card:\n  title: >-\n    [Graph.delete_node()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n    .doc-label-method} | EdgeCase\n  description: Delete a node from the graph.\ntitle: >-\n  [Graph.delete_node()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n  .doc-label-method}\nbody-classes: doc-api-page doc-py-api-page\nshift-heading-level-by: 0\nbread-crumbs: false\ntoc-depth: 3\ndescription-meta: Delete a node from the graph.\npage-navigation: false\nhtml-table-processing: none\n---\n\n::: {.doc-subject}\n\nDelete a node from the graph.\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-usage-source}\nUsage\n\n[Source](https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase/blob/main/python/edgecase/graph.py#L2901-L3023){target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"}\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-signature .doc-function}\n```pythonsignature\nGraph.delete_node(node)\n```\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-text}\n\n![Delete node](../assets/graphs/delete-node.light.svg){.lightbox fig-alt=\"Before: in a four-node cycle, node D is highlighted in the accent color along with its two incident edges. After: D and both of its edges are gone, shown as dashed outlines, leaving the path C, A, B.\" width=\"100%\"}\n\nRemoves a node and all its incident edges from the graph. The node can be specified by its\nID or label.\n\nEvery edge that starts or ends at the node is removed too (including self-loops and\nparallel edges), since an edge can't exist without both endpoints. The remaining nodes keep\ntheir IDs, and the deleted ID is not reused for nodes added later. The graph is modified in\nplace, and the deletion is recorded in the step log (see `steps`). If the node was\nselected, it is also dropped from the node selection, and its removed edges are dropped\nfrom the edge selection.\n\nUse it to prune individual nodes, e.g., removing an outlier, an isolated node or a known\nhub before re-running an analysis. To delete many nodes at once based on a condition,\nselect them and call `delete_nodes_ws()` instead. Note that removing a node can split the\ngraph into several components.\n:::\n\n## Parameters {.doc-parameters}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code>[node]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [Union[int, str]]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   The node to delete, given as an integer node ID or a string label. If a label is used\n    and several nodes share it, only the node that the label resolves to is removed.\n:::\n\n## Returns {.doc-returns}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code> [Graph]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   Returns self to enable method chaining.\n:::\n\n## Raises {.doc-raises}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code> [NodeNotFoundError]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   If the node doesn't exist in the graph (either an unknown label or an unknown ID).\n    It is a subclass of `KeyError` (which this method has always raised) and of\n    `ValueError`.\n:::\n\n## See Also {.doc-see-also}\n\n[](`~delete_nodes_ws`) \n\n:   Delete the selected nodes.\n\n[](`~delete_edge`) \n\n:   Remove an edge, keeping its nodes.\n\n[](`~add_node`) \n\n:   Add a node.\n\n## Examples {.doc-examples}\n\nDeleting a node also removes every edge incident to it. Here, \"B\" is the middle of a\nthree-node path, and deleting it leaves \"A\" and \"C\" with no edges at all:\n\n::: {#c3b351c7 .cell execution_count=1}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nimport edgecase as ec\n\ngraph = ec.Graph.from_edges([(\"A\", \"B\"), (\"B\", \"C\")])\ngraph.delete_node(node=\"B\")\n\ngraph.count_nodes(), graph.count_edges(), graph.has_node(node=\"B\")\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=1}\n```\n(2, 0, False)\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\nNodes can also be deleted by internal ID rather than label:\n\n::: {#2b5f8082 .cell execution_count=2}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\ngraph = ec.Graph().add_node(label=\"Alice\")\nnode_id = graph.get_id_from_label(label=\"Alice\")\ngraph.delete_node(node=node_id)\n\ngraph.has_node(node=node_id)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=2}\n```\nFalse\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\nDeleting a node that doesn't exist raises a `KeyError`:\n\n::: {#f22b57ec .cell execution_count=3}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\ntry:\n    graph.delete_node(node=\"Zed\")\nexcept KeyError as e:\n    print(e)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-stdout}\n```\nNode with label 'Zed' not found in graph\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\n### Closing an account\n\nIn `payments()`, Max is paid by Acme and by his flatmate Nia, and pays Nia, the Grocer\nand the Landlord. Closing Max's account takes those five payments with it, and the graph\nfalls into two pieces:\n\n::: {#78a14895 .cell execution_count=4}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\npayments = ec.payments()\nbefore = payments.count_edges()\n\npayments.delete_node(\"Max\")\n\nlost = before - payments.count_edges()\n\nlost, payments.count_weakly_connected_components()\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=4}\n```\n(5, 2)\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\nMax was the only account that paid the Landlord, which is now left with no payments at\nall:\n\n::: {#9a6c7dc9 .cell execution_count=5}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\npayments.plot(highlight=\"Landlord\", label_by=\"label\", seed=3)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=5}\n```{=html}\n<div class=\"ec-theme\" style=\"display:contents\"><style class=\"ec-theme-vars\">:where(.ec-theme){--ect-3239c383:#fafafa;--ect-e5dfd507:#94a3b8;--ect-8a2de1d4:#374151;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(15,23,42,0.88);--ect-21ade003:#f1f5f9;--ect-61169ea5:#c2410c;--ect-63cc1385:#d4d4d8;--ect-879b7ebc:#949497;--ect-b9f8de6d:#872d08;--ect-f59ba8df:#a1a1aa}@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark){.ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#0d1117;--ect-e5dfd507:#4b5563;--ect-8a2de1d4:#d1d5db;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(241,245,249,0.92);--ect-21ade003:#0f172a;--ect-61169ea5:#f97316;--ect-63cc1385:#3f3f46;--ect-879b7ebc:#2c2c31;--ect-b9f8de6d:#ae500f;--ect-f59ba8df:#71717a}}:is(html.quarto-light, body.quarto-light, html[data-bs-theme=\"light\"], [data-jp-theme-light=\"true\"], body.vscode-light, body.vscode-high-contrast-light, html[theme=\"light\"]) .ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#fafafa;--ect-e5dfd507:#94a3b8;--ect-8a2de1d4:#374151;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(15,23,42,0.88);--ect-21ade003:#f1f5f9;--ect-61169ea5:#c2410c;--ect-63cc1385:#d4d4d8;--ect-879b7ebc:#949497;--ect-b9f8de6d:#872d08;--ect-f59ba8df:#a1a1aa}:is(html.quarto-dark, body.quarto-dark, html[data-bs-theme=\"dark\"], [data-jp-theme-light=\"false\"], body.vscode-dark, body.vscode-high-contrast:not(.vscode-high-contrast-light), html[theme=\"dark\"]) .ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#0d1117;--ect-e5dfd507:#4b5563;--ect-8a2de1d4:#d1d5db;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(241,245,249,0.92);--ect-21ade003:#0f172a;--ect-61169ea5:#f97316;--ect-63cc1385:#3f3f46;--ect-879b7ebc:#2c2c31;--ect-b9f8de6d:#ae500f;--ect-f59ba8df:#71717a}</style><div class=\"ec-plot\" style=\"position:relative;width:fit-content;max-width:100%;margin:1em auto\">\n<style>.ec-plot > svg { display:block; max-width:100%; height:a